# Vigilantia configuration example.
# scripts/check_ibm_access.py, scripts/run_qpu.py, and scripts/run_qpu_external.py read the
# IBM_QUANTUM_* keys from .env. The Flask service reads the VIGILANTIA_*_PATH keys from the
# process environment. DATA_DIR, MODEL_DIR, and REPORTS_DIR are proposed.
# Copy this file to .env for future local configuration; .env is ignored by Git.
# Uncomment and adapt values only when the corresponding settings are implemented.
# Never put real credentials, personal records, or breach samples in this template.
# Copying this file does not start the API or provision AWS resources.
# python-dotenv reads this file (src/config/env_file.py); terminal-session variables take precedence.

# Proposed local application settings
# APP_ENV=development
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# API_PORT=8000

# Results service (implemented): read from the process environment, not from this file.
# VIGILANTIA_RESULTS_PATH=./reports/benchmark-results.json
# VIGILANTIA_REPLAY_PATH=./reports/benchmark-replay.json
# VIGILANTIA_EXTERNAL_PATH=./reports/external-validation.json
# VIGILANTIA_EXTERNAL_QPU_PATH=./reports/external-qpu-subset.json
# VIGILANTIA_CHART_PATH=./docs/benchmark-results.svg
# VIGILANTIA_COMPARISON_CHART_PATH=./docs/model-comparison.svg
# See docs/service.md#configuration.

# Proposed local path keys (the directories exist; these keys are not read by the code)
# DATA_DIR=./data
# MODEL_DIR=./artifacts
# REPORTS_DIR=./reports

# IBM Quantum settings. scripts/check_ibm_access.py, scripts/run_qpu.py, and
# scripts/run_qpu_external.py read them from .env; variables set in
# the terminal session take precedence. Without a token, the saved Qiskit account is used.
# The hardware scripts pass these values to QiskitRuntimeService.
# IBM_QUANTUM_TOKEN=replace-locally-with-your-token
# IBM_QUANTUM_INSTANCE=replace-with-your-open-plan-instance-crn
# IBM_QUANTUM_BACKEND=replace-with-an-accessible-backend (required by run_qpu.py and run_qpu_external.py, e.g. ibm_fez)
# Confirm the Open Plan instance and remaining quota before submitting any jobs.
# Use job mode; do not switch to a paid instance automatically.
# Hardware execution is required for the benchmark, not for local simulator checks.

# Optional future AWS deployment: replace placeholders before use.
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=replace-with-your-region
# S3_BUCKET_NAME=replace-with-your-private-bucket
# Use the AWS credential provider chain locally and task roles on AWS.
# Do not commit access keys. Local simulator experiments do not require AWS
# or IBM Quantum credentials.
